Wait For New Counters Data Frame Generation
    [Documentation]  Waits until next measurement to get new BTS Counter time frame (on default SCF configuration it
    ...              generates every 15 minutes - in case of different value, please adjust data_frame_interval keyword
    ...              argument) so counters verification will have clear data to verify.
    ...              ARGS:
    ...              - data_frame_interval (int or str):  data measurement interval defined in minutes, equal to single measurement frame duration.
    ...                                                   Related to SCF configuration. One of following values possible to set:
    ...                                                   5min, 15min, 30min, or 60min. Parameter can be provided also as integer, e.g. 15.
    ...                                                   Defaults to 15min.

    [Arguments]                                      ${data_frame_interval}=15min
    ...                                              ${return_datetime_with_local_timezone}=${False}

    Robot Log Operation                              Waiting until next measurement to get clear PM Counter time frame...
    ${start}=                                        measurements_timer.get_datetime_of_next_measurement_frame
    ...                                              measurement_interval=${data_frame_interval}
    ...                                              add_local_timezone=${return_datetime_with_local_timezone}
    measurements_timer.wait_for_measurement          datetime_of_measurement=${start}
    Robot Log Result                                 Done, test case starts.
    [Return]                                         ${start}

Wait For BTS Counter Data Frames Generation
    [Documentation]  Waits specified time for BTS Counter data frames to generate since the beginning of the Test Case.
    ...              Default data frame generation time is 15 minutes (one data frame per quarter), so keyword
    ...              will perform sleep operation for remaining time since `start` argument, e.g.
    ...              start argument: 2020-07-03 15:15:30, execution time of keyword: 2020-07-03 15:24:30 then
    ...              6 minutes sleep will be performed (up to 2020-07-03 15:30:30).
    ...              IMPORTANT! An additional 3 min wait is added to the waiting time as counters may appear in webem
    ...                         with delay
    ...              ARGS:
    ...              - start (datetime):  date and time of measurement frame start
    ...              - time (int or str):  duration (in minutes) of overall measurement
    ...              - data_frame_interval (int or str):  data measurement interval defined in minutes, equal to single measurement frame duration.
    ...                                                   Related to SCF configuration. One of following values possible to set:
    ...                                                   5min, 15min, 30min, or 60min. Parameter can be provided also as integer, e.g. 15.
    ...                                                   Defaults to 15min.
    [Arguments]                                      ${start}
    ...                                              ${time}
    ...                                              ${data_frame_interval}=15min

    ${count_of_measurement_frames}                   measurements_timer.get_count_of_measurement_frames_based_on_overall_time
    ...                                              measurement_time=${time}
    ...                                              measurement_interval=${data_frame_interval}

    ${stop}                                          measurements_timer.get_datetime_of_the_end_of_measurements
    ...                                              measurements_start=${start}
    ...                                              measurement_interval=${data_frame_interval}
    ...                                              count_of_measurement_frames=${count_of_measurement_frames}

    @{current_time}                                  Get Time
    ...                                              hour min sec
    Robot Log Operation                              Waiting until ${stop} for last counters frame generation...
    Robot Log Operation                              Current time is: ${current_time[0]}:${current_time[1]}:${current_time[2]}

    measurements_timer.wait_for_measurement          datetime_of_measurement=${stop}

    Robot Log Result                                 Done, BTS counters frames have been generated!

Wait for End of Current Counters Frame and Collect Counters
