Verify SCF Parameters Responsible For Counters Collection
    [Documentation]  Verifies whether SCF parameters responsible for counters collection are set to expected values.
    ...              Keyword fails if any parameter value does not match the expected one.
    ...              ARGS:
    ...              - expected_parameters_values_dict (dict): dictionary with parameter names as keys and expected values as values,
    ...                                                        e.g. {'pmCollectInterval':'15min', 'pmEnable':'true'}
    ...              - parameters_distname (str): distname where parameters are located, e.g. 'MRBTS-{}/NRBTS-{}/NRPMRNL-1'
    ...              - connection (str): connection alias to use for configuration operations
    [Arguments]                                      ${expected_parameters_values_dict}
    ...                                              ${parameters_distname}
    ...                                              ${connection}

    Robot Log Operation                              Verifying SCF parameters responsible for counters collection...

    config_operations.connect                        alias=${connection}
    FOR      ${param_name}  ${expected_value}  IN    &{expected_parameters_values_dict}
        ${current_param_value}=                      config_operations.get_parameter_value
        ...                                          dist_name=${parameters_distname}
        ...                                          param_name=${param_name}
        Should Be Equal                              ${current_param_value}    ${expected_value}
        ...                                          msg=Parameter '${param_name}' value verification failed! Expected: '${expected_value}', Actual: '${current_param_value}'
    END

    Robot Log Result                                 SCF parameters verification successful!
